          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زبادي (zabādī) is a modern word for yoghurt. It may be linked with the root z-b-d, which gives zubd, \"fresh butter\", and zubād, \"thin milk\" (Lane), but its formation is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
